<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kemah</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kemah is a small town on the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erzincan">Erzincan</a> province, eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, below a strong fortress on a rock above the river gorge. Known in Byzantine times as Kamacha, it was one of the seats of the Mengujekid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">emirs</a> from the late eleventh century, and later passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>.</p></div>
